h builds a new obs with no `uuid`, and the stored obs was never voided. Every save added another obs for the same question, even if the value was never edited.\r\n\r\nThis was most visible on date fields with a `calculateExpression` or `defaultValue`, because the engine runs `transformFieldValue` on those fields on load, and again whenever a field they depend on changes. It also happened when a user edited a field and then changed it back, re-selected the same coded answer, or re-toggled a toggle to its stored state.\r\n\r\nDate fields had a second problem. `hasPreviousObsValueChanged` compared `date` fields with `dayjs.diff(..., 'D')`, but dayjs does not support `'D'` in `diff` and falls back to milliseconds. So a time-only difference on a `calendar` field counted as a change even though the submitted day was the same, while a sub-minute difference on a `datetime` field counted as no change and then hit the duplicate path above.\r\n\r\nThe changes that went into the fix (all in `src/adapters/obs-adapter.ts`):\r\n\r\n1. `transformFieldValue` returns early when a field has a stored obs and its value is unchanged, so nothing is submitted for it.\r\n2. `hasPreviousObsValueChanged` formats the stored value and the new value with `formatDateByPickerType`, the same function `editObs` and `constructObs` use, and compares the strings. A date now counts as changed exactly when the submitted value would change, at the precision of the field's `datePickerFormat`.\r\n3. `formatDateByPickerType` falls back to the transformer's defaults (`both` for `datetime`, `calendar` otherwise) when a field has no `datePickerFormat`, instead of returning the raw `Date`.\r\n4. `getPreviousValue` no longer treats the previous encounter's obs as the field's own obs. When a form shows the patient's answer from their previous encounter (`historicalExpression` or a previous encounter), the engine loaded that obs as if it belonged to the current field. So if the user changed or cleared the value in the new encounter, the engine sent an update or void for the previous encounter's obs, and the backend voided the answer in the previous encounter. Now the previous answer is only used as a value, and a changed or reused value is saved as a new obs in the current encounter. This had to change here, because with the early return in (1), a reused value would otherwise count as unchanged and not be saved at all.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n\r\n[https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5847](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5847)\r\n\r\n## Other","freshness":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","lastSyncedAt":"2026-10-31T16:11:00.658Z","stale":false}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89d08702-4fd8-4ab1-a429-5b837b9d401c","uuid":"4e478538-65e4-4082-987c-2431a481b605","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:12:18.373Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","number":842,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) O3-5847: Stop unchanged obs values from creating duplicate obs","state":"merged","author":"NethmiRodrigo","createdAt":"2026-10-12T13:48:08.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-10-13T10:47:06.000Z","closedAt":"2026-10-13T10:47:06.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/pull/842","mergeCommit":"b0d8fd2e9a0c68f2c72b2415b6dbf351b6e92c30","syncedAt":"2026-10-31T16:11:00.658Z","tickets":[{"key":"O3-5847","source":"ticket-pattern"}],"commits":[{"sha":"b0d8fd2e9a0c68f2c72b2415b6dbf351b6e92c30","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"src/adapters/obs-adapter.test.ts","additions":398,"deletions":7},{"path":"src/adapters/obs-adapter.ts","additions":26,"deletions":20},{"path":"src/processors/encounter/__snapshots__/encounter-payloads/edit-encounter-obs-changes.json","additions":0,"deletions":6},{"path":"src/processors/encounter/encounter-payloads.golden.test.ts","additions":108,"deletions":62}],"body":"